// The action schema writes an attribute name with a JSON-style escape, `"\u00c4"`, which Cedar's
// schema syntax does not have, and the policy puts an array in a temporal predicate argument. The
// public pipeline fails first at the derivation of the event signatures, which parses the action
// schema; the export's stages that need the schema do not run, and the array check, which does
// not, fails. The frontend harness's `export` check counts the schema's rejection where the
// pipeline meets it.
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"Read", resource)
when temporal {
    formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"Login"::response{ input.user: ["a", "b"] }
};
